Captain Endo, played by Masanori Mimoto.

11
00:56:30,000 --> 00:56:36,000
Prisoner of War (formerly titled Death March) is a 2025  martial arts war film directed by
Louis Mandylor and written by Marc Clebanoff, based on a story by Scott Adkins.

12
01:01:38,181 --> 01:01:44,181
The film features Adkins alongside Peter Shinkoda, Donald
Cerrone, Michael Copon, and Gabbi Garcia.

13
01:06:46,363 --> 01:06:52,363
Produced by Odyssey Motion Pictures and distributed by Well Go USA Entertainment, it
combines martial arts action with a World War II prisoner-of-war narrative.

14
01:11:54,545 --> 01:12:00,545
It premiered at the Beverly Hills Film Festival in April 2025 and had a limited
theatrical and digital release in the United States on September 19, 2025.

15
01:17:02,727 --> 01:17:08,727
Set during the Battle of Bataan, the plot centers on British RAF officer Wing Commander James Wright
(Adkins), who is captured by Japanese forces and confined to a harsh POW camp in the Philippines.

16
01:22:10,909 --> 01:22:16,909
There, Wright is forced into hand-to-hand combat
matches for his captors’ amusement.

17
01:27:19,090 --> 01:27:25,090
Using his prior martial arts training, he motivates resistance among
fellow prisoners while devising a bold escape plan.

18
01:32:27,272 --> 01:32:33,272
The film received mixed to positive critical feedback, with praise for Adkins’s performance and the
fight choreography, though the narrative depth and supporting characters faced criticism.

19
01:37:35,454 --> 01:37:41,454
Reviewers highlighted its fusion of war epic and martial arts elements,
with some calling it a raw, visceral take on the genre.

20
01:42:43,636 --> 01:42:49,636
The film explores themes of world war ii, prisoner
of war, internment camp, 1940s.

21
01:47:51,818 --> 01:47:57,818
The tone is dark and intense.
